A||||14||CUTTER||MSD Ignition stuff||||1||
Z||000000||CUTTER||10-03-1999||02:02 AM||||Hey today I ordered a MSD cap and rotor, and MSD sparkplug wires. and getting splitfire plugs. What do you think would be the HP gain on this stuff?<BR> Thanks again, Shane||||reg||1
Z||000001||mshill||10-03-1999||02:58 AM||||Shane,<P>Unless your cap is corroded or cracked and your wires are arcing and your plugs are fouled, you won't see a gain in HP.  If you haven't done a tuneup lately you might notice that it runs a little smoother.  Otherwise, it will be negligible.<P>You might want to search the archives for peoples experience with SplitFire plugs, from what I have read it isn't good with the DIS ignition in the L4.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-03-1999||09:06 AM||||Most ignition system power gains are up in the high RPM range where the old stock stuff starts getting weak. You might be aware that the company that makes those Splitfire plugs have lots of lawsuits pending because their product does not live up to their claims.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88 Fiero||10-03-1999||11:14 AM||||Shane...if you are going to replace your spark plugs don't buy the Splitfires...they are bogus plugs...Buddies of mine tested the SplitFires and they don't show what they are advertising...the spark was very, very poor...Instead buy the Bosch +4 plugs which has 4 tips for better sparking or GM also came out with a Spark Plug that has a Ring on the tip for better sparking...||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||10-03-1999||01:13 PM||||I have used Accel plugs in all my high performance engines during the last 20 years and never had a problem.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||10-03-1999||01:51 PM||||I think the Accel plugs are made by Nippondenso,those or NGK are what I buy.<P>My stock coil (bone-stock'87 V6)must not be all that weak;I took out some AC plugs last night that had a gap of 1/8" and it didn't run any better with new,gapped plugs.(?)||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||10-04-1999||09:52 AM||||I bought my 87 v6 last summer, and decided last month it needed a tune up.  Judging by the looks of the three plugs that face forward, they were the original plugs.  They were pretty well rusted in place.  <P>I was surprised that the car really did not run bad at all, and all I really noticed was a bit smoother idle.  Those original plugs must have been pretty good plugs.  <P>I like the Bosch Platinums.  They dont cost 4 bucks a pop, and in my experience, they hold up well.<P>Thats my .02  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||Greg Piet||04-14-2000||03:23 PM||||I too have an MSD ignition system, but I couldnt find the proper MSD rotor and cap for the 2.8 distributor(i found the v8 one)...   Would someone be so kind as to tell me the MSD part numbers?||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||04-14-2000||04:16 PM||||The purpose of tune-up items is to obtain optimal performance from your car, not necessarily to gain horsepower.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Greg Piet||04-14-2000||04:25 PM||||I just ressurected this thread with my question so if someone else does a search under MSD it is more compact.<BR>I am not looking to give my car 300hp with a MSD cap, but revamping the thread for the following reason. <BR>I had a Borg Warner cap and the center electrode went away after about 500 miles...<BR>So I wanted to get an MSD cap instead of replacing the cap every 500 miles.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ka4nkf||04-14-2000||07:27 PM||||I sent a E-mail to MSD and they told me they did not make a cap and rotor for the fiero, so I got a wells cap and rotor.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Capt Fiero||04-14-2000||07:57 PM||||MSD makes an awsome blaster coil for the V-6 it works very well. I and 3 other club members use it.  Much better idle and smoother power curve up into the 6000 rpm range.  Not anymore power it just helped smooth the weak coil out.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||ka4nkf||04-14-2000||09:06 PM||||I have the MSD blaster coil and it sure does make a difference in how it runs. lots smoother. well worth the money.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Greg Piet||04-15-2000||12:25 AM||||Ok <BR>I have the 6AL (PN 6420)<BR>the GM Blaster coil (PN 8226)<BR>the adjustable rev limiter from about 4600 to  6800 (PN 8671)<BR>The wiring harness (PN 8876).<BR>MSD Heli Coil wires (PN 3116)<P>I made a bracket to mount the GM Blaster coil, so I can switch directly back to stock whenever I decide.  I took pics but they are on my friends computer.<BR>I thought the camaro 2.8  v6 used the same distributor, and MSD might have it under that listing...    So far I have heard that a Wells cap a rotor did the job...  Where is the best place to get one of those(Checker only carries Niehoff and Borg Warner?<BR>I will attest that a Borg Warner cap does not cut the mustard.||||reg||1
Z||000014||ka4nkf||04-15-2000||08:54 AM||||I got my wells cap and rotor at Autozone.<BR>part no. #DR2012G.||||reg||1
